              "exam_name": "NEET 2018 · NCERT",
              "question": "<p>The nitration of aniline in a strong acidic medium results in the formation of m-nitroaniline because:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>In spite of substituents, the nitro group always&nbsp;goes to only the m-position.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>In electrophilic substitution reactions, the amino group is meta-directive.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>In the absence of&nbsp;substituents, the nitro group always&nbsp;goes to only m-position.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td>In an acidic (strong) medium, aniline is present&nbsp;as an anilinium ion.</td></tr></tbody></table>",
